        "procedure": "Triethylamine (0.2 mmol) was added to a stirring solution of Gd(NO3)3·6H2O (0.1 mmol, 0.0452 g), ZnCl2 (0.1 mmol, 0.0136 g), HL (0.1 mmol, 0.0243 g), and sodium pivalate (Napiv) (0.1 mmol, 0.0142 g) in mixed MeOH/MeCN (1:1, 20 mL) at room temperature. The yellow solution was stirred for 4 h, filtered, and the filtrate was left undisturbed to evaporate slowly. X-ray quality crystals grew over several days and were collected by filtration and washed with MeOH.",
